######################
## Traffic Settings ##
####################################################################################################
#                                                                                                  #
# Traffic Manager:                                                                                 #
#                                                                                                  #
# This will allow you to specify Min/Max speed for users/paths.                                    #
#                                                                                                  #
# Note: This plug-in works on a first match system.                                                #
# IE. If you are part of 2 types, only the least most number type will engage.                     #
#                                                                                                  #
# x.type = Traffic Type to use.                                                                    #
# x.name = Name of this type.                                                                      #
# x.minspeed = Min speed allowed for this type (In KB/s) (0 for Disable).                          #
# x.maxspeed = Max speed allowed for this type (In KB/s) (0 for Disable).                          #
# x.include = Regex format to Include Paths for this Type (All = *).                               #
# x.exclude = Regex format to Include Paths for this Type.                                         #
# x.perms = Permissions for this Type.                                                             #
# x.up = Use this type for Upload (True/False).                                                    #
# x.dn = Use this type for Download (True/False).                                                  #
#                                                                                                  #
# - Default:                                                                                       #
#                                                                                                  #
# This will just stop/throttle the transfer.                                                       #
#                                                                                                  #
# - Kick:                                                                                          #
#                                                                                                  #
# This will kick the user for a slow transfer.                                                     #
#                                                                                                  #
# x.reason = Kick reason.                                                                          #
#                                                                                                  #
# - Ban:                                                                                           #
#                                                                                                  #
# This will ban the user for a slow transfer.                                                      #
#                                                                                                  #
# x.reason = Ban reason.                                                                           #
# x.bantime = Time in seconds to ban user (Default 300).                                           #
# x.kickall = Kick all connections or just current (True/False) (Default true).                    #
#                                                                                                  #
# - Dual (opt-in, only active when a x.type=Dual entry exists below):                              #
#                                                                                                  #
# Detects a user running several simultaneous transfers of the SAME release directory, each        #
# faster than x.minspeed (dualing). Uploads and downloads are counted separately. The action       #
# is applied to the most recently started transfer, once per user/release per x.cooldown.          #
# The "release" is the parent directory of the transferred file: CD1 and CD2 (or release and its   #
# Sample dir) are different releases and are counted separately.                                   #
# Dual entries never limit speed and never affect the other types (they are not first-match).      #
# A Dual entry is skipped (and logged) if minspeed is 0, perms is empty or neither up/dn is set.   #
#                                                                                                  #
# x.action = default (announce only), kick or ban (same extra keys as those types).                #
# x.limit = Simultaneous transfers that trigger (Default 2, minimum 2).                            #
# x.cooldown = Seconds before the same user/release can be actioned again (Default 60).            #
# x.takecredits = Credits to take in KB on detection (Default 0 = none).                           #
# x.perms = Who it applies to; '!' entries first exempt users/groups ('!=staff *').                #
# x.exclude = Regex of paths (sections) that are exempt.                                           #
#                                                                                                  #
# Example below the box (uncomment to enable).                                                     #
#                                                                                                  #
####################################################################################################


# Dual example (off by default): kick a user (except staff) who uploads 2+ files of the same release
# at once, each above 500 KB/s, in /MP3 (not in /MP3/PRE). Use x.action=default to only announce.
#1.type=Dual
#1.name=NoDualing
#1.action=kick
#1.reason=Dualing is not allowed
#1.minspeed=500
#1.up=true
#1.dn=false
#1.limit=2
#1.cooldown=60
#1.perms=!=staff *
#1.include=/MP3/.*
#1.exclude=/MP3/PRE/.*
